  "question": {
    "text": "A body released from a great height falls freely towards the earth. Another body is released from the same height exactly one second later. The separation (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>) between the two bodies two seconds after the release of the second body is (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "24.5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Separation of the body after&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> second after the release of 1st body is<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>g</mi><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>g</mi><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>9.8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>"
